# Change password from the Options menu, not forced: each local
# refusal, a wrong old password, then success and a login with the new
# password.
T READER
K TAB
T Reader1986
K ENTER
S P0
K ALT-O P
S P1
# the new password and its repetition differ
T Reader1986
K TAB
T Newpass1
K TAB
T Newpass2
K ENTER
S P2
K ESC
S P3
# too short
K ALT-O P
T Reader1986
K TAB
T abc
K TAB
T abc
K ENTER
S P4
K ESC
# a bad character, the blank
K ALT-O P
T Reader1986
K TAB
T new pass
K TAB
T new pass
K ENTER
S P5
K ESC
# the same as the old one
K ALT-O P
T Reader1986
K TAB
T Reader1986
K TAB
T Reader1986
K ENTER
S P6
K ESC
# a wrong old password reaches the server
K ALT-O P
T Wrongold1
K TAB
T Newpass1
K TAB
T Newpass1
K ENTER
S P7
K ESC
# success: the dialog closes
K ALT-O P
T Reader1986
K TAB
T Newpass1
K TAB
T Newpass1
K ENTER
S P8
# log out, and in again with the new password
K ALT-F L
S P9
T Newpass1
K ENTER
S P10
K ALT-F X
